://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107728.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"Fixes #107510\r\n\r\nNormally, clicking a \"rotate left\" or \"rotate right\" button for a tile in a grid would rotate it 90 degrees. This was fine for square tiles, but would make hexagonal tiles not fit the grid properly. This PR makes hexagonal tiles only rotate 180 degrees when the button is pushed, so it still fits. (making them rotate by 60 degrees would have been ideal, but comes with additional complications).","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107728/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107728/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}